  "text": "Skip to content\nFully insured shipping\nAuthenticity guaranteed\nWe buy it back\nNYC Diamond District counter\nSecure checkout\nPAMP 1.5 Oz Silver Lady Liberty 999 Fine Coin Solomon Islands\nby\nPAMP\n✓ LBMA Good Delivery\n$\n105.36\nPriced live off the spot market.\nSee price history ↓\nMetal\nSilver\nWeight\n1.5 oz Troy Ounces\nPurity\n99.9\nType\nCoin\n82 In stock\nQty\nQuantity\nCheck/Wire\nCrypto\nCard/Paypal\n1-9\n1 - 9\n0%\n$\n106.09\n$\n108.21\n$\n111.39\n10-99\n10 - 99\n0.05%\n$\n106.04\n$\n108.16\n$\n111.34\n100+\n100 +\n1%\n$\n105.03\n$\n107.13\n$\n110.28\nAdd to wishlist\nGo to compare\nAdd to compare\nFully insured shipping\nShips in 1–3 business days\nWe buy it back —\nsell to us\nSecure checkout · NYC Diamond District counter\nSKU:\nS15oLLSOL\nCategories:\nSilver\n,\nSilver Coins\nMint:\nPAMP\nPrice history\nPAMP 1.5 Oz Silver Lady Liberty 999 Fine Coin Solomon Islands was last recorded at $106.09 on October 10, 2026. Over the past 12 months it is up 24.9% and has ranged between $79.87 and $194.91.\nLast recorded\nLoading…\n1Y\n7D\n1M\n3M\n6M\n1Y\nAll\nDescription\nAdditional information\nDescription\nCommemorate the iconic Statue of Liberty with this 1.5 oz silver coin from the Bavarian State Mint. Featuring a close-up depiction of Lady Liberty’s head on the reverse and the effigy of Queen Elizabeth II on the obverse, this 999 fine silver coin is a timeless addition to any collection. Designed by renowned French sculptor Auguste Bartholdi, the Statue of Liberty stands as a symbol of freedom, democracy, and the American spirit. This coin is shipped in an assay card, providing authenticity and protection for your precious metal investment.\nThis 1.5 oz silver coin features 999 Fine Silver\nThe reverse of the coin depicts a close-up of the head of the iconic Statue of Liberty\nThe obverse features an effigy of Queen Elizabeth II, her name, the artist’s initials, the year of release, the name of the country of issue, the face value of the coin, and the metal weight, type, and purity\nThe Statue of Liberty was designed by French sculptor Auguste Bartholdi, with the framework provided by Gustave Eiffel\nThe Statue of Liberty was proposed to embody the spirit of freedom, democracy, and liberty, the quintessential ideals of America\nThe monument was designed and sculpted within France and shipped to the United States as an acknowledgment that their newly formed ideas were supported\nThe Statue of Liberty stands tall as a beacon of hope to the rest of the world, as the entry point to the land of opportunity.\nComes in original packaging. A great addition to your bullion collection.\nAdditional information\nType of Bullion\nCoin\nProduct Type\nlegal_tender_coin\nIssuer Country\nOther\nIs Legal Tender\nYes\nIs Monetized Bullion\nNo\nPurity %\n99.9\nMetal\nSilver\nWeight\n1.5 oz\nWeight Unit\nTroy Ounces\nRelated products\nOut of stock\nRead more\nSilver\n,\nSilver Coins\n,\nUS Silver Coins\nSilver Peace Dollars(Random Year)\n$\n54.52\nRead more\nQuickview\nGo to compare\nAdd to compare\nQty\nAdd to cart\nChinese Silver Pandas\n,\nGovernment Mint Silver Coins\n,\nSilver\n,\nSilver Coins\n1 oz Silver Chinese Panda Coins Random Years\n$\n77.73\nQty\nAdd to cart\nQuickview\nGo to compare\nAdd to compare\nQty\nAdd to cart\n5 oz Silver Bars\n,\nGifts\n,\nSilver\n,\nSilver Bars\n,\nSilver Bullets for Sale\n5 oz Silver Bullet\n$\n386.23\nQty\nAdd to cart\nQuickview\nGo to compare\nAdd to compare\nQty\nAdd to cart\n5 oz Silver Bars\n,\nSilver\n,\nSilver Bars\n5 oz Secondary Market Silver Bars(Random Brand)\n$\n328.63\nQty\nAdd to cart\nQuickview\nGo to compare\nAdd to compare\n$\n105.36\nAdd to cart\nLogin/Register\nDon't have an account\nRegister\nCustomer Login\nIf you have an account, sign in with your email address.\nContinue with Google\nLoading\nYour Cart\nCart is Empty\nUpdating Cart!\nHowdy,                             Guest\nSign in\nDepartments\nShop\nMints\nCart\nMy Account",
